---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import '../../styles/lab.css';
---
<SiteLayout title="Research — Worldeology Lab" description="The Worldeology Lab research map: mind inference, metacognitive control, and consequential world models." headerTone="paper" active="research" image="/og.png">
  <main id="main" class="lab-site lab-page">
    <header class="lab-page-hero"><p class="lab-index">Worldeology Lab / Research</p><h1>From mind<br />to world.</h1><p>Our work follows one cognitive trajectory across three research problems: infer what is hidden before action, inspect what changes during reasoning, and model what grows after an action enters the world.</p></header>

    <section class="lab-page-section" aria-labelledby="core-title"><header><p class="lab-index">01 / Core program</p><h2 id="core-title">Three coupled research questions.</h2></header>
      <div class="research-map">
        <article><span>Mind inference</span><h3>What does another agent believe, need, intend, or withhold?</h3><p>We build explicit, revisable models of latent social state under ambiguity, norms, roles, and incomplete evidence.</p><a href="/blog/MetaMind/technical-contribution/">MetaMind research release ↗</a></article>
        <article id="metacognition"><span>Metacognitive control</span><h3>Where did a reasoning trajectory begin to diverge?</h3><p>We study process-level inspection, reflective decoding, rollback, constraint-aware refinement, and learned cognitive control.</p><a href="/blog/MetaMind/cognitive-frontier/">Cognitive frontier ↗</a></article>
        <article><span>Consequential worlds</span><h3>What future becomes reachable after the system acts?</h3><p>We model latent-state change, causal event chains, durable memory, relationships, institutions, and long-horizon consequences.</p><a href="/projects/mariolm/">MarioLM dossier ↗</a></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="lab-page-section" aria-labelledby="adjacent-title"><header><p class="lab-index">02 / Adjacent research</p><h2 id="adjacent-title">Mechanisms and evaluation that make the program possible.</h2></header>
      <div class="lab-principles">
        <article><b>01</b><h3>Model mechanisms</h3><p>Layer dynamics, test-time computation, and inference-time intervention reveal where capabilities form and where alignment perturbs them.</p></article>
        <article><b>02</b><h3>Long-horizon safety</h3><p>Deception, persuasion, preference change, and trust cannot be evaluated reliably in a single isolated turn.</p></article>
        <article><b>03</b><h3>Social simulation</h3><p>Controllable agents and persistent worlds make counterfactual consequences observable, testable, and trainable.</p></article>
        <article><b>04</b><h3>Trustworthy evaluation</h3><p>Fresh tasks, causal traces, capability decomposition, and human calibration keep measurement connected to real failure.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="lab-page-section" aria-labelledby="papers-title"><header><p class="lab-index">03 / Work index</p><h2 id="papers-title">Projects, papers, and working systems.</h2></header>
      <div class="work-list">
        <a class="work-row" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.18943"><span>NeurIPS</span><div><b>Spotlight · 2025</b><h3>MetaMind</h3></div><p>Social cognition</p><i>↗</i></a>
        <a class="work-row" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.23441"><span>ACL</span><div><b>Long paper · 2026</b><h3>Cognition-of-Thought</h3></div><p>Reflective reasoning</p><i>↗</i></a>
        <a class="work-row" href="/projects/mariolm/"><span>System</span><div><b>Active research · 2026</b><h3>MarioLM</h3></div><p>Interactive worlds</p><i>↗</i></a>
        <a class="work-row" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.03999"><span>ICLR</span><div><b>2026</b><h3>Long-Horizon Deception</h3></div><p>AI safety</p><i>↗</i></a>
        <a class="work-row" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.21906"><span>System</span><div><b>2026</b><h3>Confident Decoding</h3></div><p>Model mechanisms</p><i>↗</i></a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <SiteFooter />
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
